        <headline>High Wind Warning issued September 26 at 1:17PM EDT until September 26 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...North winds 20 to 30 mph with gusts up to 60 mph.

* WHERE...Delaware Beaches County.

* WHEN...Until 6 PM EDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.
Widespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult,
especially for high profile vehicles.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...While there may be a lull in winds later today
into this evening, winds are expected to increase again overnight
into Sunday morning.
</description>
        <instruction>People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around
or damaged by the wind.</instruction>
